      "content": "For reducing direct physical contact that might transfer micro-vibrations or heat, you could consider sitting on a supportive, breathable cushion made of natural, porous materials like bamboo or high-quality cotton. These materials can act as a slight insulator and dampener between your body and the chair's structure. Furthermore, consciously trying to maintain light, consistent body weight distribution across the entire seat area can minimize focal pressure points that might trigger sensors.",
